The permission rules in `.claude/settings.json` name the plugin cache path (`…/hakanserce-plugins/atm/*/scripts/atm …`): don't edit settings; list the lines that need the new name in the task's outcome note for Hakan to change.

Hakan finds the task detail panel's vertical scrollbar (when a task's details don't fit) out of place in the dashboard's look. Done live with him: try, look, adjust.

## Change
- **No scrollbar**: the sections scroll like the Kanban columns (`KanbanScroll.svelte`, T-262): hidden scrollbar, the wheel and trackpad scroll as usual, "▲ N more" / "▼ N more" hints (sections cut off) that scroll a page.
- **The title and badges stay** at the top, the × on the title's line; less padding around the panel.
- **A section rail on the left**: one entry per group, written bottom to top, with an icon; a click brings the group to the top (just below the "▲" hint), adding empty space below the last section when the content is too short; scrolling by hand never adds any, and scrolling back up takes it away. The entry of the group in view is highlighted. Groups (only those the task has):
  - *Info*: in review / blocked, description;
  - *Dependencies*: Depends on, Required by (one line each; a long name ends in "…");
  - *Notes*;
  - *Activity*: claimed by, who, timestamps, commit;
  - *Ref*: use cases, requirements, files.
- Only the task panel (`#detail-panel`): Help, About, the Activity popup and What's new share `.detail-panel` and keep their layout.

## Tests
Component tests for the rail's groups and order, e2e tests for where a rail click lands and the active entry on a short task, the detail specs on the new scroller (`#detail-body`), refreshed detail screenshot baselines.

`atm components add` (T-324) refuses a component already there, so a second label can't be moved onto an existing component. Add `atm components edit <id>` with the same options, for an existing one, in one locked write:
- `--label TEXT` sets the name shown (empty: remove it); `--review MODE` its review mode (empty: remove it);
- `--add-path GLOB` (repeatable) adds globs (one already there is kept once);
- `--from-label LABEL` moves the label onto it on every task, `tasks.json` and `tasks-archive.json`, and drops it from `meta.labels` (as `add` does);
- `--assign` gives it to every task whose `files` its globs match, the new ones included.

It refuses an unknown component (naming the components), a bad glob or mode, and a label no task has (a typo), writing nothing; it prints what changed, e.g. `cli: 6 tasks from the label atm-cli, 2 more by their files`. Share the label-moving and assigning code with `components_add` rather than copying it.

## Tests
Scenarios in `tests/scripts/scenarios/components.json`: edit with each option, the archive too, the refusals.

## Docs
`docs/v4/atm-cli.md`, the usage text, `plugin/CLAUDE.md`'s *Define* line if it names the subcommands, `plugin/CHANGELOG.md`.

Finish what T-325 started, with `atm components add` and `edit` (run from this checkout, `plugin/scripts/atm`, until 0.25.0 is installed):
- **cli**: `edit` with `--from-label atm-cli`;
- **api**: `edit` with `--from-label server`;
- **ci** (*CI*): `add` with `.github/**`, `.githooks/**`, `--from-label ci`, `--assign`;
- **branding** (*Branding*): `add` with `branding/**`, `dashboard/src/assets/**`, `--from-label branding`, `--assign`;
- **docs** (*Docs*): `add` with `docs/**`, `README.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `--assign` (not `plugin/CHANGELOG.md` or `plugin/WHATS-NEW.md`: every release task touches them; decided with Hakan).

The other labels (features, topics, kinds of work) stay labels. Check with `atm components` and `atm check`, then commit `tasks.json` (and the archive if it changed) on its own: `chore: this repository's remaining components`.

The Task List is one card per row, so most of each row is empty. Show more of the task there (`TaskCard.svelte`), choosing with Hakan on the dev server.

## Candidates
- the first line or two of the description (plain text, `markdownPlainText`);
- who created it, who works or worked on it, and when (created, started, done, relative times as elsewhere);
- how long it took (work time) or how long it has waited (in review, blocked);
- its stage with the commit or PR link, its dependencies and what waits for it;
- the latest note (outcome, handoff) in one line.

## Layout
A right-hand column for the facts (people, times, stage) and the left for the name, chips and description, collapsing to today's single column on narrow windows. Cards stay quick to scan; no new data loads.

## Tests
TaskCard component tests for the new fields; the List screenshots updated; the performance budget still holds (`tests/e2e/performance.spec.ts`).

T-412 work item 3, [improving-atm-cli-ergonomics.md](docs/improving-atm-cli-ergonomics.md) §4.5 and §4.8. The commands people and agents use (`task`, `loop`, `claim`, `sprint`, `release`, `component`, `project`, `vcs`) stay at the top of `atm2 --help`; the ones git, hooks and the server call go out of the way:

- `merge-driver` (git runs it) as `db merge-driver`, hidden; `db init` registers it, as now;
- `heartbeat --auto` stays the hook's entry point;
- `paths` is `project config`; `summary` (the dashboard's dev server reads it) goes under `project`, hidden;
- `version` and `help` as top-level meta commands.

Update the command tree and the old→new table (§8) in the doc.

[ADR-003](docs/adr/ADR-003-workspaces.md) §1 and §4, step 2.

## Change
- **The project's settings file**, `.agentic-task-manager/settings.json` (`store`, `vcs`; json-git and git without one), read before any store is chosen.
- **Factories:** `atm_db::open(folder, store)` and `atm_vcs::open(folder, vcs)`. Finding a project from a folder (walking up, a linked worktree's main copy) moves behind the store's factory.
- **atm-lib:**
  - `Project::open(cwd)`;
  - `Project::with_store(store, vcs)` for tests;
  - `project.store_maintenance()` (merge driver, migrations, paths; `None` for a store without them);
  - the actor.
- **`Workspaces`** (over atm-db's `workspaces/<id>.json` and `recent.json`, under the state folder's lock) and **`Workspace`**:
  - its projects, with summaries, worktrees and logos, a broken one listed as missing (F18);
  - search across them;
  - add, remove and prune;
  - the summary cache, moved from atm-api's `Projects`.
  - A new project atm meets goes into `default`.

atm-api's `Projects` calls these instead of its own loop; nothing users see changes.

## Tests
atm-lib's unit tests on the in-memory store through `with_store`; the scenarios and `serve.test.mjs` unchanged and passing.

The spike of [the desktop app design](docs/app-desktop-ui-design.md) [§2](docs/app-desktop-ui-design.md#2-the-title-bar) and §6, on Windows 11 and on Linux (X11 and Wayland, GNOME): with the page's own title bar (`decorations: false`), check
- Windows 11's snap layouts from the page's maximize button;
- resizing the window from its edges;
- the system window menu (Alt+Space on Windows);
- the menu's accelerators firing while the native menu is hidden (`hide_menu`).

Record the results in the design doc. Where one can't be had without a hack, switch that platform to the system's title bar with the same two rows under it (the decided fallback); if the accelerators don't fire, the page handles those keys from the menu's definition.

Follow-up of T-483 (in-app updates, approved), done with Hakan when 0.36.0 (or the first release after 0.35.0) is published.

## Check
On a Mac with 0.35.0 installed (one from the release download, one from the Homebrew cask, which says `auto_updates true`):
- the app offers the update and asks before installing (never silently);
- the download's signature is verified against the built-in key (a tampered or wrongly signed archive is refused: check on a draft release, if practical);
- it installs, restarts on the new version, and the bundled `atm` is the new one too (`atm version`);
- `brew upgrade` afterwards leaves the cask's app alone.

Record the result in a note; a problem becomes a task.
